            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="PAT02" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Samuel</forename>
                        <surname>Paterson</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1728">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1802"/>
                    <occupation>Bookseller and auctioneer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>See Ed Pope notes: Paterson (Coryat) was certainly Samuel Paterson DNB
                            1728-1802 who used the pseudonym Coryat for his Another Traveller! 1767.
                            He died from a fall on 29.11.1802 so could have also been the next two
                            Paterson entries at Johnson's in 1799 and 1802. We have made a separate
                            entry for Col Paterson - (who appears in 1798) but it is then unclear to
                            whom entries prior to 1802 refer; and also unclear to whom references
                            post 1802 are. (Col Paterson was Daniel
                            Paterson DNB 1738-1825).</p>
                    </note>
